course: dictionary
lesson: 1744
title: The clarinet and its family
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A clarinet is a woodwind instrument. It is a long, black tube with keys, and at the mouthpiece a single reed vibrates when you blow to make its smooth, warm sound.
explain: «The saxophone is made of brass but is a woodwind, because it makes its sound with a reed, like a clarinet.» The sentence shows that instruments are grouped into families by how they make sound, not only by what they are made of.
explain: The clarinet is in the woodwind family with the flute, oboe and bassoon. Many children learn it in school bands and orchestras, and a person who plays it is a clarinet player, or a clarinettist.
fact: A clarinet is a woodwind instrument shaped like a long black tube with keys.
fact: It has a single reed in the mouthpiece, and it makes a smooth, warm sound.
fact: The woodwind family includes the flute, oboe, bassoon and clarinet.
fact: Phrases you may hear in music class are «play the clarinet» and «clarinet lessons».
fact: The clarinet is used in jazz and classical music.
exercise: What kind of instrument is a clarinet? | A brass instrument with valves | A string instrument played with a bow | *A woodwind instrument, shaped like a long black tube with keys | A drum played with sticks
exercise: «The saxophone is made of brass but is a woodwind, because it makes its sound with a reed, like a clarinet.» Which other instrument in the sentence makes its sound with a reed? | A trumpet | A drum | A cymbal | *A saxophone
exercise: Which instruments belong to the same woodwind family as the clarinet? | Violin, cello, harp | Trumpet, tuba, horn | *Flute, oboe, bassoon | Piano, drum, guitar
test: What does a clarinet's mouthpiece contain? | No reed at all | Two reeds | A bow | *A single reed
test: Which phrase would you hear in a music lesson? | clarinet rope | clarinet football | *clarinet lessons | clarinet kitchen
exam: What is a person who plays the clarinet called? | *Clarinettist | Clarinet maker | Woodcutter | Reedman
